  "narrative": {
    "intro": "North Carolina received $296M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The federal government issued 4,500 awards in the state, with an average award size of $65.7K. Obligations fell 94.9% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show prior-year totals of $8.6B in FY22, $7B in FY23, $7.2B in FY24, $9.4B in FY25, and $5.8B in FY26. The Department of Agriculture led buying in FY2027 to date with $107M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $69.6M and the General Services Administration with $31M. PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC received the largest vendor total at $99.6M. Logging is the largest industry by obligation at $99.6M, followed by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $26.2M and Computer Systems Design Services at $24.1M. The current-year totals are partial because figures are fiscal year to date. This snapshot highlights a sharp year-over-year decline in obligations alongside concentration in a few buyers, vendors, and industries.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How big is the drop in federal contracting activity in North Carolina this fiscal year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 94.9% year over year. North Carolina recorded $296M in FY2027 to date compared with prior fiscal-year totals of $5.8B in FY26 and larger totals in earlier years. The count of awards was 4,500 with an average award size of $65.7K, reflecting lower total obligations this fiscal year. The current-year totals are partial, so the FY2027 to date figure represents fiscal year to date obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, vendors, and industries dominate federal contracting in North Carolina right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Agriculture obligated $107M and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $69.6M in FY2027 to date. PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC received $99.6M and Logging recorded $99.6M in obligations, making both the top vendor and top industry by dollar value. The General Services Administration obligated $31M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction recorded $26.2M in obligations. Computer Systems Design Services recorded $24.1M in obligations, showing a mix of construction, logging, and IT spending."
      }
    ]
  },
